    "explanation": "The SGD 4.00 no-show fee charged on trip TRP-00619 (EV-FARE-00619, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued 0.00) is refunded in full to the rider.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand. A no-show fee is chargeable only if the driver actually reached the pickup point. The pickup is a LARGE_VENUE zone (EV-TRIP-00619), so under POL-NS-02 the driver is deemed to have arrived only if the trace holds at least three consecutive fixes within 120 m of the pin. His own 67-fix trace (EV-GPS-00619, 100% coverage, no gaps, 0.0 s max gap) contains 0 qualifying fixes: his closest approach to the pin over the entire run was 263.97 m — more than twice the radius — and the trace shows no in-geofence run at all (longest 0.0 s). POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails and the fee is not chargeable. Independently, POL-NS-06 refunds the fee on a waiting-period shortfall: the effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 s against the 300 s minimum for LARGE_VENUE — a shortfall of 300.0 s — and that clause refunds whether or not the rider was present or responded to messages.\n\nThe driver's arguments. POL-NS-03 (wrong-entrance) does not assist: it requires the driver to have held position outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin for the 300 s dwell, and the trace shows him moving at speeds up to 56.9 km/h with no such stationary hold, so the SGD 2.00 pin-ambiguity goodwill under POL-NS-03(ii) is not payable. The 'GPS in that estate is bad' explanation is not available either: the trace has full coverage and no gaps, and fixes worse than 25 m would count as evidence of neither presence nor absence. On POL-NS-05, the driver's nearest recorded fix (263.97 m) is inside the clause's 300 m line and the brief does not place him beyond 300 m at the 06:34:52 arrival marker, so the marker is not shown to be false and no false-arrival record is entered in referrals. POL-NS-04 exonerates no one on these facts: the driver answered the rider's 06:36:10 message at 06:36:40, 30 s later and well inside the 120 s window, and had already placed an answered 110 s in-app call at 06:35:40, so limb (b) fails on either branch.\n\nThe rider's arguments. Her device sat at the pin across the whole window (48 fixes, 06:34:40 to 06:41:43, mean 8.01 m from the pin, 0.0 km/h throughout), contradicting the RIDER_NO_SHOW code recorded under POL-NS-01(d) and confirming that the failure was the driver's arrival, not her absence. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not, and the anti-farming test is not reached (1 no-show termination against 110 completed trips in 30 days would not trip it in any event).\n\nEvidence integrity. No limb of POL-NS-08 is engaged: the 'arrived' event is 2 s from the nearest trace fix (threshold 90 s), there is no sampling gap over 120 s, the chat log holds the 2 messages the trip record records, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation line equals the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) under the resolution rule. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts stands at weight 1.0, so confidence is not capped and no limb of POL-NS-09 escalates the case."
