    "explanation": "To both parties: the dispute is over the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged to the rider (EV-FARE-00619: cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). That fee is refunded in full.\n\nThe charge cannot stand under POL-NS-01, which needs all four limbs. Limb (b) requires the GPS trace to place the driver inside the pickup geofence — 120 m for this LARGE_VENUE pickup at The Cascadia guardhouse — at or before the 06:34:52 'arrived' event. The driver's own 67-fix trace (EV-GPS-00619, weight 1.0) reports 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes (qualifying_fix_count 0) and a closest approach of 263.97 m, more than twice the radius. Limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least 300 s; the measured dwell is 0.0 s, a shortfall of 300.0 s. With limbs (b) and (c) failing, POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 each direct a full refund, and POL-NS-06 refunds the fee 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages' — so neither the rider's presence (48 qualifying fixes, mean 8.01 m from the pin, stationary) nor the driver's reply and 110-second answered call rescues the charge.\n\nThe driver's account that 'GPS in that estate is bad' is not available on this record: EV-GPS-00619 has 100.0% coverage, no gaps and a 0.0 s maximum gap, and the 25 m accuracy filter cannot move a 263.97 m nearest fix inside a 120 m radius.\n\nOn the wrong-entrance argument: the pickup carried 2 registered pickup points and the driver's closest approach of 263.97 m sits inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling, so POL-NS-03 governs the fault allocation — and it gives the rider the same full refund. The driver's claim for the pin-ambiguity goodwill (SGD 2.00, 50% of the SGD 4.00 fee) is rejected: limb (ii) applies only where NEITHER party specified a sub-location, and the rider's 06:36:10 message named where she was ('I'm at the front gate, the pin is the guardhouse'). Under limb (i) the rider gave a locating statement and the driver did not move to it before cancelling at 06:41:50, so the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation.\n\nNo driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it; it is not satisfied, and POL-NS-06 displaces it. (For completeness the anti-farming check does not trip: 1 no-show termination in 30 days against 110 completed trips.)\n\nNo POL-NS-08 impairment arises, so this is a full refund and not a partial one: the 06:34:52 arrival event is 2 s from the nearest fix (inside the 90 s skew tolerance); the trace has no gap over 120 s; the chat holds 2 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 2; and the SGD 4.00 line equals the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00). The deciding facts rest on artifacts at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00619-01, weight 0.0) matters only to POL-NS-06(i) aggregation, which is not reached because there is no in-geofence interval to sum.\n\nThe rider's separate POL-NS-04 claim is not needed and was correctly not pressed: the driver replied within 120 s and had already called, so that clause does not exonerate her; the refund comes from the arrival and dwell failures. The driver's POL-NS-05 point is accepted — the closest fix (263.97 m) is inside the 300 m line, so the arrival marker is not shown to be false and no false-arrival referral is recorded. No clause produces a referral here, and no escalation ground is met (confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the profiles show 0 cross-party disputes and 0 relevant counters, and the trace is unimpaired). One rider claim was discarded at the citation stage for not disclosing the missing advisory's impairment, and nothing is built on it.",
